{"url":"https://github.com/ChengshuLi/WorldAtlas/issues/954","title":"Resolve US ADM2 source hash lineage and dated coastal boundary differences","issue_number":954,"body":"2026-10-06 (America/Los_Angeles), post-merge Auditor update: **ready for the existing bounded source research**. #432 is closed and its canonical reservation is released. The earlier “blocked until merge” wording below is preserved as dated history. The catalog digest's full-versus-simplified meaning is now established; use the evidence below instead of treating it as an unexplained stale hash. Coastal history and the exact 216-ID source-to-Atlas processing remain research questions. No shared data edits or geographic approval are authorized.\n\nParent: #432. Bounded source-lineage and historical-boundary evidence follow-up; maximum 1 focused PR. This issue is blocked until #432 is independently reviewed and merged so the original scope and evidence packet remain stable. It does not certify West South Central or authorize any shared data changes.\n\n## Owned scope\n\nOnly the exact 216 #432 location IDs in the appendix below, concerning the `gb:USA:ADM2` source lineage and the eight coastal comparison signals listed here. The source-catalog discrepancy may have wider relevance; this issue makes no claims about unlisted entities. The declared owned path is `data/regional-review/usa-adm2-lineage-432/`.\n\nOriginal source artifact retrieved from the entry's own pinned `gjDownloadURL`: `https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/USA/ADM2/geoBoundaries-USA-ADM2.geojson`; resolved commit `9469f09592ced973a3448cf66b6100b741b64c0d`; response SHA-256 `81fdd384df8012e5007ed2994a8ab306352f3c48e32cd8ea99182195e8647f43`. `data/administrative-sources.json` currently records SHA-256 `16249e8d795aaded6a72910a8c72115a073814b25ee902d61ccc9a9490c6641a` for `gb:USA:ADM2`. The meaning/revision of that discrepancy is unresolved. Do not overwrite the shared pin without discovering what bytes/serialization it identifies.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Reproduce the original catalog SHA claim against authoritative build/release files or document its precise unresolved cause; record exact source hash, URL, retrieval date, source vintage, completeness and license evidence.\n- Retrieve and preserve the matching official Census 2018 TIGER county/equivalent vintage and the dated 2018–2025 boundary-change material relevant to the eight listed units. Hash source bytes and provide lawful retention or restoration instructions.\n- Compare each of the 216 Atlas geometries against its exact raw 2018 GeoBoundaries feature and determine whether the coordinate differences have a documented transformation/generalization process; preserve separate source-to-Atlas and Atlas-to-current measurements.\n- For each of the eight exact county IDs, assess whether its geometry difference from 2025 Census TIGER reflects documented boundary change, shoreline/water treatment, generalization, or remains unknown. Cite the exact records and dates; do not treat overlap thresholds as legal proof.\n- Classify every exact member individually as justified, correction-needed, or insufficient-evidence for source/boundary status. Explain why this class is distinct from the county-tier/name/parent support in #432.\n- Provide a clear engineering handoff. No Atlas/core geography edits, shared source catalog mutations, production records, release/publication, historical imports, deployment, or region certification.\n- Run exact source-hash reproduction, membership/scope checks and the required independent review. Close only this bounded follow-up when its acceptance is met; it cannot approve the whole West South Central area or regional branch.\n\n## Eight high-difference county-equivalent signals from #432\n\n| Atlas ID | Census GEOID | Name | IoU vs TIGERweb 2026 | Symmetric difference km² |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| `gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B18014802865122` | `22109` | Terrebonne | 0.72320915 | 1496.4249