:USA:ADM2:52423323B82335716857681\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B82358250228718\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B82500281635270\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B82644020143866\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B82661835696463\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B82795635342125\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83046273754506\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83070703413565\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83124951000608\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83504400209000\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83678883467317\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83762983029089\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B83994293092269\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B84636308996882\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B84660675823799\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B84817986944382\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B85918245780607\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B86572463849564\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B87068688197244\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B87929534363237\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B90005102118407\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B90141807319554\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B90433618963574\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B90681107174232\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B91280713828925\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B91358685939419\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B91490874625057\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B9154242656865\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B92257960877908\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B92305544895329\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B92446440923992\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B9246238437830\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B93240032804570\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B93386698636065\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B93718948099955\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B93993712170814\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B94132750651187\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B95130922587904\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B95239416662840\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B9748869428654\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B97917914395582\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B98282084999585\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B98678441689198\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B99086550227942\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B99277183073993\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B99576880853175\",\"gb:USA:ADM2:52423323B99692802996111\"],\"pins\":{\"atlas_part_25\":\"dada55df1b7f0f2a2b307f4aea071d0e48791e3105875755fe74a292a6763394\",\"atlas_part_26\":\"44de5da3531f5641e0496ab7b01ed73871b40705e2a3eafdda470926872b6632\",\"atlas_part_27\":\"e8df7555853e9262162c5e5d5c85e5c30be3fa8f0e6339bafec0e08323054758\"},\"review_kind\":\"geometry\"}}\n-->\n\n\n## Post-merge audit evidence for #958 — 2026-10-06\n\nAuditor `01a10892-0782-7b13-902c-d8b4db6c155d`; original PR [#958](https://github.com/ChengshuLi/WorldAtlas/pull/958), immutable merge `3a00e68b6e64ff8945d9f89a8215f8f2c9159b15`; baseline `c6ae0ee321135335f49031eba5d4b51adb3794bf`. Evidence prefix: `data/regional-review/regional-review-6fce33d53fdff81e/`. This adds evidence and precise restoration criteria without changing the exact subjects, owned path or one-PR budget.\n\n### Catalog digest: resolved representation distinction\n\nThe earlier conclusion that the catalog hash's meaning is unknown is outdated. At the immutable #958 merge, `scripts/administrative.py` downloads `row['simplifiedGeometryGeoJSON']` into `.cache/geoboundaries/USA-ADM2.json` and hashes that file for `sources['gb:USA:ADM2']['sha256']`. Feature provenance separately cites `gjDownloadURL`, the full-resolution source. Authenticated GitHub contents at upstream commit `9469f09592ced973a3448cf66b6100b741b64c0d` prove:\n\n- `releaseData/gbOpen/USA/ADM2/geoBoundaries-USA-ADM2_simplified.geojson`: LFS SHA-256 `16249e8d795aaded6a72910a8c72115a073814b25ee902d61ccc9a9490c6641a`, 7,938,450 bytes — exactly the catalog digest.\n- Full-resolution `geoBoundaries-USA-ADM2.geojson`: LFS SHA-256 `81fdd384df8012e5007ed2994a8ab306352f3c48e32cd8ea99182195e8647f43`, 10,500,644 bytes — exactly the retained full source.\n\nThis distinction was also documented in later [#989](https://github.com/ChengshuLi/WorldAtlas/pull/989), merge `c42f4b7465964245ecbcd8eed4961eb76af3106b`, closing [#981](https://github.com/ChengshuLi/WorldAtlas/issues/981) for a different 279-ID scope. The Auditor independently hashed its retained 7,938,450-byte simplified file and 939-byte upstream metadata against the actual upstream pointers. Both full and simplified files have 3,233 unique shapeIDs; all this issue's 216 identities resolve uniquely with matching names. The simplified file still differs structurally and topologically from every scoped frozen Atlas shape; minimum projected IoU is 0.9832500346212951. Thus the checksum meaning is resolved, but this is not complete proof of all source-to-Atlas processing or present-day boundary accuracy. Reuse #989's immutable source evidence; do not repeat its completed 279-ID research or change the shared catalog hash. #989 remains separately auditable.\n\n### Confirmed restoration URL defect\n\n`source-inventory.json`, source `census-tigerweb-counties-2026`, field `feature_query_url`, uses `%26` in place of query-parameter delimiters. Local URI parsing returns only `where`, whose value includes `&outFields=*&returnGeometry=true&outSR=4326&f=geojson&orderByFields=STATE,COUNTY`. Those are not distinct URL parameters. This fails to encode the recorded request and can defeat restoration; no live Census request was executed by the Auditor.\n\nReproduction: parse that inventory URL with `urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlparse(url).query)` and compare with `sources/census-tigerweb-2026/retrieval-receipt.json` → `county_query.url`. The latter correctly separates `where`, `outFields`, `returnGeometry`, `outSR`, `f`, and `orderByFields`. Expected behavior is an exact, separately parameterized restoration request for the retained 216-feature response and its documented output CRS. Preserve the original packet; carry the correction and original receipt reference into the new owned research output. Success requires the corrected request to parse into exactly the recorded parameters and restore/verifiably identify the intended artifact rather than claiming a successful live test that was not performed.\n\n### Independent verification and remaining source scope\n\nAll 24 changed files are ordinary bounded files; all head/merge bytes agree (42,602,255 bytes), and all 23 declared payload checksums match. Two isolated executions of the inspected comparator wrote only private scratch; all four generated outputs matched each other and retained bytes exactly. The 216 unique current-code joins split 75 Arkansas / 64 Louisiana / 77 Oklahoma; all state prefixes and three parent inventories match the pinned baseline. Raw-to-Atlas IoU ranges 0.98305974–0.99976855, with 15 below 0.99; Atlas-to-retained-2026 minimum is 0.30169002, with 37 below 0.98. All 216 boundary classifications remain insufficient-evidence. The nine retained 2025 samples comprise the eight named coastal targets plus Arkansas County control; minimum sample-to-2026 IoU is 0.999999997. Eight multipart baseline units are a screen, not an omission finding. Name-only Lafayette lookup is ambiguous between GEOIDs 22055 and 05073; state-qualified joins distinguish them. Independent wrong/missing-state and duplicate-match controls reject ambiguity; planar rectangle IoU and EPSG:5070 origin controls pass.\n\nThe retained 175-page 2025 Census technical PDF was inspected for county-equivalent roles, Figure 15, vintage and restrictions (PDF pages 12, 19, 37–38; pages 12 and 37 also rendered). It supports Louisiana parishes at the county-equivalent tier, Census reuse/attribution, and January 1, 2025 representation. It expressly does not provide jurisdiction/ownership or legal land-description determinations. The 83,989,800-byte national TIGER archive exceeds the review cap and was not restored/decompressed; derivation of the nine-feature excerpt from that full archive remains independently unchecked. Retained live-service captures were inspected but not re-fetched under the GitHub-only access restriction. No legal-history/coastal difference or regional approval is established by these screens.\n\n### Pins, readiness and success criteria\n\nAt baseline `c6ae0ee321135335f49031eba5d4b51adb3794bf` (unchanged at #958 merge), the existing named SHA-256 pins mean whole files:\n\n- `atlas_part_25` → `data/geography/part-25.json`, SHA-256 `dada55df1b7f0f2a2b307f4aea071d0e48791e3105875755fe74a292a6763394`.\n- `atlas_part_26` → `data/geography/part-26.json`, SHA-256 `44de5da3531f5641e0496ab7b01ed73871b40705e2a3eafdda470926872b6632`.\n- `atlas_part_27` → `data/geography/part-27.json`, SHA-256 `e8df7555853e9262162c5e5d5c85e5c30be3fa8f0e6339bafec0e08323054758`.\n\nThe Auditor checked actual input bytes, exact 216 subjects/containing files, the valid work contract, closed #432 dependency and released reservation, complete open/closed issue pagination, and all current open PR file lists. No active claim or overlapping `data/regional-review/usa-adm2-lineage-432/` work was found. Marked ready only for source research in that owned path. Preserve the original packet, IDs and dates. The existing acceptance remains required; its hash-lineage portion should explicitly reuse the proven full/simplified distinction. Explain the remaining transformation provenance and each dated coastal question individually; retain lawful bounded authoritative source evidence or honest restoration limits; correct the new output's restoration request; keep unsupported conclusions unresolved. No core edits, publication, import or geography approval. A worker must separately reserve this ready issue before implementation/research.\n\n\n## Supplemental audit of completion PR #961 — 2026-10-06\n\nAuditor `01a10892-0782-7b13-902c-d8b4db6c155d`; merge `c89bd7384b295da221a76a8dbf375adff431ab0a`. PR #961 adds `acceptance-audit.md` and one checksum binding, closes #432, and preserves all earlier packet sources, comparison outputs and Atlas input bytes. The Auditor independently checked all 24 payload bindings and 28 unchanged packet/baseline files against its earlier two complete #958 comparison runs. Exact live issue scope remains 216 unique IDs (75 Arkansas, 64 Louisiana, 77 Oklahoma); all individual classifications remain insufficient-evidence. No new execution is claimed for #961: the prior independent execution is bound to exactly identical merged inputs/outputs.\n\nThe acceptance statement still says catalog-hash meaning is unresolved. Use the established distinction above: actual source preparation downloads and hashes `simplifiedGeometryGeoJSON`, while feature provenance cites the full-resolution `gjDownloadURL`. Fresh authenticated upstream GitHub contents at `9469f09592ced973a3448cf66b6100b741b64c0d` confirm simplified digest `16249e8d795aaded6a72910a8c72115a073814b25ee902d61ccc9a9490c6641a`, 7,938,450 bytes, and full digest `81fdd384df8012e5007ed2994a8ab306352f3c48e32cd8ea99182195e8647f43`, 10,500,644 bytes. Preserve the original dated statement and explain this resolved distinction in the child output. Remaining source-to-Atlas transformation and dated coastal history must stay separate questions; changing the catalog hash would discard valid provenance.\n\nThe malformed restoration URL also remains in the immutable #961 source inventory. Re-parsing gives only the `where` parameter; parsing the actual retained receipt gives the six intended parameters. The defect, reproduction and success criteria above continue to apply; no live Census failure or successful restoration is asserted.\n\n#961's audit remains Incomplete because the national 83,989,800-byte 2025 TIGER archive exceeds the 32 MiB ordinary/decompressed-file cap and the nine-feature excerpt ancestry was not independently established; retained live-service capture ancestry was not refetched under the GitHub-only access restriction. Provide lawful bounded primary/restoration evidence and dated history or precise remaining limits, preserving all subjects, parts, older results and source vintages. This does not claim a legal-boundary defect from an IoU screen.\n\nFresh complete open/closed issue pagination, the entire open PR file list, current closed #432 dependency/released canonical reservation and this child's absence of a reservation were checked. Its exact 216-subject scope, whole-file part pins, one-PR budget, ready urgent/follow-up geography labels and owned output path remain unchanged. No duplicate issue or active owned-path overlap was found.\n","state":"open","user":{"login":"ChengshuLi","name":"ChengshuLi","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6732996?v=4","id":6732996},"assignees":null,"labels":[{"name":"kind:work-item","color":"0e8a16","description":"Bounded actionable scope, normally 1–3 PRs"},{"name":"status:ready","color":"0e8a16","description":"Reviewed scope and dependencies ready for a worker claim"},{"name":"type:geography","color":"8250df","description":"Geographic source research, hierarchy/boundary evidence and proposals; no live mutations"},{"name":"urgent","color":"ededed","description":null},{"name":"follow-up","color":"ededed","description":null},{"name":"priority:follow-up","color":"ededed","description":null}],"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-05T12:14:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T10:41:03Z","closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/ChengshuLi/WorldAtlas/issues/954","display_title":"Resolve US ADM2 source hash lineage and dated coastal boundary differences"}